# Critical rules — verify before every response

## Forbidden actions

- Never run shell commands or terminal commands (user has sole discretion)
- Never make code changes without explicit user request
- Never assume work is complete without verification
- Never create generic folders like `controllers/`, `views/`, `services/`
- Follow **`comments.mdc`** for in-source comments and TSDoc; **`documentation.mdc`** for READMEs and `docs/`
- Never include HTML/SCSS directly in TypeScript components (use separate files)

## Required actions

- For checklist-backed multi-step work, follow **`checklist-discipline.mdc`**: one row at a time (read → fix → `[x]` before the next row); if the user says checklist items were missed, recover from the first `[ ]` in order without rebuilding the list
- Always answer questions directly before taking action
- Always verify changes by reading the actual file output
- Always use standalone Angular components with separate template/stylesheet files
- Always use explicit `this.` where applicable for instance members
- Always use braces `{ }` for all control structures, even single-line blocks
